{
  "company_name": "FreshStock Solutions",
  "industry": "Food & Beverage",
  "use_case": "Perishable food inventory optimization and shelf life management",
  "space_title": "FreshStock Solutions - Perishable Inventory Optimization 📦",
  "space_description": "**Subindustry:** Food & Beverage\n\n**Use case:** Perishable Inventory Optimization & Shelf-Life Management\n\nFreshStock Solutions — perishable inventory analytics across 20 SKUs and 12 production lines balancing freshness, spoilage cost, and customer fill-rate commitments. Plant Managers and Supply Chain leaders use this space day-to-day to monitor on-hand, days-to-expiry, and FIFO compliance; the S&OP team and CFO use it to quantify shrink, drive inventory turnover, and protect retailer OTIF scorecards.\n\n**Key KPIs**\n- Spoilage rate (%) — fresh produce ~5-8%, refrigerated ~5%, dry goods <2% benchmark\n- Fill rate (%) — retailer scorecard threshold 95-98% OTIF\n- Freshness score — blended quality / days-remaining index 0-100\n- Total spoilage cost ($) — shrink dollars; perishables drive ~2/3 of grocery shrink\n- Average shelf remaining (days) — pipeline health for downstream channels\n- Inventory turnover ratio — target 12-20x annually for fresh items\n- Near-expiry units — at-risk inventory needing markdown or diversion\n- On-hand units — stocking-position balance vs. expected demand\n\n**Data sources**\n- `perishable_products` — daily inventory movements with quantity, days-to-expiry, temperature zone\n- `inventory_transactions` — weekly snapshots with on-hand, near-expiry, spoilage rate, fill rate, freshness\n- `shelf_life_snapshots` — monthly waste-reduction rollup with spoiled units, spoilage cost, turnover, optimization action",
