  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports Perishable Inventory Optimization for a multi-category food manufacturer / distributor managing bakery, dairy, produce, protein, seafood, and frozen SKUs against tight retailer fill-rate SLAs. Stakeholders include the Plant Manager and Supply Chain leader (daily on-hand, days-to-expiry, FIFO), the S&OP team (turnover, demand-vs-supply balance), and the CFO (shrink dollars, working capital). Optimization_action is Reorder / Markdown / Hold / Divert.\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- Spoilage rate = AVG(spoilage_rate_pct); benchmark <2% dry, ~5% refrigerated, 5-8% fresh produce\n- Fill rate = AVG(fill_rate_pct); 95-98% OTIF target for retailer scorecards (Walmart, Kroger)\n- Freshness score = AVG(freshness_score); composite 0-100 quality / days-remaining index\n- Total spoilage cost = SUM(spoilage_cost_usd); ~2/3 of grocery shrink comes from perishables\n- Average shelf remaining days = AVG(avg_shelf_remaining_days)\n- Turnover ratio = AVG(turnover_ratio); fresh items target 12-20x annual, premium fresh 26-52x\n- Near-expiry units = SUM(near_expiry_units); at-risk inventory needing intervention\n- On-hand units = AVG(on_hand_units); stocking-position health\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - inventory_kpi_monthly (source: inventory_transactions) — dims: snapshot_date, product_category, production_line; measures: avg_on_hand, avg_spoilage_rate, avg_fill_rate, avg_freshness, total_near_expiry, unique_product_count, max_on_hand_units.\n  - waste_kpi_monthly (source: shelf_life_snapshots) — dims: perf_month, product_category, optimization_action; measures: total_spoiled, total_spoilage_cost, avg_turnover, avg_shelf_remaining, item_count, max_total_spoiled_units.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. product_id, product_name, days_to_expiry, movement_type, temperature_zone).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
  "sample_questions": [
    "Show the monthly trend in total spoilage cost across all product categories for the trailing 12 months.",
    "Top 10 product categories by spoilage cost this year — what optimization actions are most common for each?",
    "Which production lines have the lowest fill rate, and how much near-expiry inventory are they carrying?",
    "How has average freshness score trended month-over-month by product category?",
    "Top 10 product categories by near-expiry units — what is the projected shrink dollar exposure?",
    "Which temperature zones in the perishable_products table show the highest spoilage and shortest days-to-expiry?",
    "What is the monthly trend in inventory turnover ratio, and which categories fall below the 12x benchmark?"
  ],
  "example_sqls": [
    {
      "question": "What is the monthly trend in total near-expiry units?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT snapshot_date, MEASURE(total_near_expiry) AS total_near_expiry",
        "FROM {fqn}.inventory_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY snapshot_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has avg units on hand changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT snapshot_date, MEASURE(avg_on_hand) AS avg_on_hand",
        "FROM {fqn}.inventory_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY snapshot_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the monthly trend in total units spoiled?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT perf_month, MEASURE(total_spoiled) AS total_spoiled",
        "FROM {fqn}.waste_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY perf_month"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the monthly trend in avg shelf life remaining days?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT perf_month, MEASURE(avg_shelf_remaining) AS avg_shelf_remaining",
        "FROM {fqn}.waste_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY perf_month"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the trend of total units moved over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT movement_date, SUM(quantity_units) AS total_quantity_units",
        "FROM {fqn}.perishable_products",
        "GROUP BY movement_date ORDER BY movement_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the trend of total units on hand over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT snapshot_date, SUM(on_hand_units) AS total_on_hand_units",
        "FROM {fqn}.inventory_transactions",
        "GROUP BY snapshot_date ORDER BY snapshot_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has the average inventory turnover ratio changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT perf_month, AVG(turnover_ratio) AS avg_turnover_ratio",
        "FROM {fqn}.shelf_life_snapshots",
        "GROUP BY perf_month ORDER BY perf_month"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "sql_snippets": {
    "filters": [
